  "answer": "In the implemented Iris protocol slice, restarting the ChatRuntime does **not** preserve conversation context or queued work. While Iris history and UUIDs survive, they are not rehydrated into the runtime context, and an application restart does not resume an outstanding turn or rehydrate state and queued work [E1]. Furthermore, a restart discards runtime sources, summaries, context, and jobs, as durable recovery and retention/deletion APIs are still considered future work [E1, E2]. \n\nRegarding the distinction between the proposal and implementation: the implementation deliberately supersedes the original ADR proposal by disabling the automatic unavailable-runtime fallback to avoid the risk of executing an accepted turn a second time [E1].",
